instructions: |
  The model says one thing: the QRH is a static site published on GitHub Pages, outside the
  homelab, so the procedures for bringing the homelab back are reachable while it is down.

  Only a change to how or where the site is published changes the architecture: the hosting, the
  URL, or a new surface people reach by name. Adding, editing or removing an SOP under sops/ never
  does, nor does a change to the site's look or to site/build.py that keeps the same surface.

  Deliberately left out: the individual SOPs and the mirrored Ansible runbooks (files), edges from
  an SOP to the things it is about (a documentation index, not architecture), the build-time
  mirror of pvginkel/Ansible (a dependency between repos), the GitHub Actions build and its daily
  schedule, the offline zip (a file on the same surface) and the checkbox state kept in the
  browser.
